+# BLOCKED: libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz does not match SHA256SUMS
+
+The release check cannot pass because one published artifact's contents do not
+match the checksum recorded in `SHA256SUMS`. This is a real integrity failure,
+not a bug in the verification script, so it must not be papered over.
+
+## Evidence
+
+```
+manifest (SHA256SUMS): 7BEE020AC21EFB3831D920AF0B8C5EFE8D44CDF227AB94847F509188420356BD
+actual (shasum -a 256): fde9b2575edbefb297fa7d93738b4bb1f09b7f777d1723b90194ad53cd9bc9ce
+file:                   artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz
+```
+
+The other two artifacts match the manifest after the verifier fixes below:
+
+```
+artifacts/cli-2.0.1.zip       61ebdff8... (manifest 61EBDFF8...)
+artifacts/docs-2026.10.tar.gz efb78462... (manifest EFB78462...)
+```
+
+## Why this is blocked
+
+- The mismatch means the artifact differs from what was signed off in the
+  manifest (corrupted, truncated, or a different build).
+- Replacing `artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` is not possible from this
+  repository: there is no source tree, build script, or other copy from which
+  to rebuild `libfoo-1.4.2`.
+- Editing `SHA256SUMS` to contain the current artifact's hash would make the
+  check pass but destroy its purpose: the manifest would no longer attest to
+  the intended release contents. That is a workaround, not a fix.
+
+## What is needed to unblock
+
+Obtain a known-good `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` whose SHA-256 is
+`7BEE020A...0356BD` (or the correct new artifact plus a regenerated,
+authoritatively signed manifest), place it in `artifacts/`, and re-run
+`python3 verify.py`.
+
+## Work completed
+
+`verify.py` was fixed for two real bugs:
+
+1. Files are now read in binary mode (`open(path, "rb")`) and hashed as bytes;
+   the previous text-mode read crashed or hashed re-encoded text for binary
+   artifacts.
+2. Manifest digests are compared case-insensitively (`expected.lower()`), since
+   `SHA256SUMS` records uppercase hashes while `hashlib` returns lowercase.
+
+After these fixes `python3 test_verify.py` gives 2 passes; the remaining
+failure is `test_release_artifacts_verify`, caused solely by the genuine
+`libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` mismatch described above.
diff --git a/verify.py b/verify.py
